    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d382">

                <pb facs="d382-01" n="1" xml:id="d382-01"/>

                <head>382. Telegram 1047 From the Department of State to the Consulate General in
                        Dacca<anchor n="1" xml:id="d382-f1"/>
                    <anchor n="2" xml:id="d382-f2"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1972-01-04"
                        >January 4, 1972, 2232Z</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>For Spivack from Secretary</p>
                <p>In view of sensitivity and fluidity of situation you should seek to avoid further
                    contact with Bangla Desh reps. If Bangla Desh reps seek appointment with you,
                    you should seek instructions from Department.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed> Rogers </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d382-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d382-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, Nixon Presidential Materials, NSC Files, Box 627,
                    Country Files, Middle East, Pakistan, Vol. IX, Jan-31 Aug 72. Secret; Priority;
                    Nodis. Drafted by Sisco, cleared by Eliot, and approved by Rogers. Repeated to
                    Calcutta, Islamabad, and New Delhi.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d382-f2" n="2" xml:id="d382-f2-content">
                <p>Secretary of State Rogers instructed Consul General Spivack to avoid further
                    contact with Bangladesh representatives.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
